recomp-kit is a static recompilation kit. Every game it builds is represented
by its own repository, which carries that game's notices. Original game names,
executable code, artwork, audio, levels and other data retain their original
ownership and notices; this project is not affiliated with or endorsed by any
game's publisher.

The handwritten native host, compatibility runtime, translator, build/test
tools and project documentation are covered by LICENSE. Generated translations
of a game's executable are local build products and are never tracked here.
A game's executable, data, artwork, audio and levels are always required from
the player's own copy and are never included.

Lua 5.4.6 is included unmodified under its upstream MIT license; see
third_party/lua/LICENSE and the notices in its source files.

Ghidra, Capstone, pefile, Unicorn, NumPy and Pillow are external development
tools with their own licenses, not game dependencies at runtime.

TinySoundFont (third_party/tsf/tsf.h) is Copyright (C) 2017-2023 Bernhard Schelling,
licensed under the MIT License; see third_party/tsf/LICENSE. It renders a game's
own SoundFont, which is not included.

SDL3 is fetched at build time from https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL at a pinned
release tag and linked statically; it is licensed under the zlib License.

volk (third_party/volk) is Copyright (c) 2018-2024 Arseny Kapoulkine, MIT License;
see third_party/volk/LICENSE.md. The Vulkan headers (third_party/vulkan-headers)
are Copyright 2015-2025 The Khronos Group Inc., Apache License 2.0 or MIT; see
third_party/vulkan-headers/LICENSE.md. Both are included unmodified. The Vulkan
